# CAFM Asset Importer — reuse the working flow

This is a **Manifest V3 Chrome extension** (plain JS, no bundler). Before writing code, read the relevant existing module and extend it.

## Architecture (do not replace)

- **Namespace**: all modules attach to `globalThis.CAFMImporter` via IIFEs (`src/bootstrap.js` → `src/content-entry.js`).
- **Load order**: `manifest.json` `content_scripts.js` array — new modules must be inserted in the correct dependency position.
- **Orchestration**: `src/workflow/engine.js` (`runAutomatic`, `scheduleAuto`) is the only automation loop. Page files handle one step, then set `session.auto.phase` and call `scheduleAuto()`.
- **Phases**: defined in `src/workflow/phases.js`. New phases must be added there, in `src/pages/registry.js`, and in `tools/verify-architecture.js`.
- **Page routing**: `src/pages/registry.js` maps CAFM page type → handler. Extend an existing handler; do not add a second router.
- **Post-save handoff**: `src/workflow/post-save.js` + `src/pages/asset-saved.js` (close editor → activate → PPM).
- **Background tabs**: `background.js` message types (`ASSET_CLOSE_EDITOR_TAB`, `EE_ASSET_EDITOR_CLOSED`, PPM parent/child close). Pair every new message with handlers in `background.js` and `src/runtime/messages.js`.

## Working flow (end-to-end — extend this, do not replace)

Reference: `ISSUE_TRACKING.md` state diagram. Each step = one handler call from `engine.js` → page module → `persistSession` → `scheduleAuto`.

### 1. Asset creation (New Entity page)

| Phase | Page | Handler | What happens |
|-------|------|---------|--------------|
| `navigate` | `ViewFASSETItem.aspx?id=-1` | `asset-new.js` | Confirm new-entity page; start fill |
| `fill` / `filling` | same | `asset-new.js` `fillCurrentRecord` | Fill tabs/lookups from workbook row |
| `saving` | same | `post-save.js` `clickSaveTracked` | Pre-save audit, click Save |
| `await_save` | same → saved URL | `engine.js` | Poll until `isSavedAssetPage()` or validation error |

On save confirmed → `post-save.js` `beginPostSave` sets phase `asset_close_child`.

### 2. Close editor + activate (Saved Asset page)

| Phase | Handler | What happens |
|-------|---------|--------------|
| `asset_close_child` | `asset-saved.js` `processAssetCloseAfterSave` | Find Close button (`toolbar.js`), click, send `ASSET_CLOSE_EDITOR_TAB` |
| `asset_close_wait` | same | Poll until tab closes; background sends `EE_ASSET_EDITOR_CLOSED` → `activate_open` |
| `activate_open` | `asset-saved.js` `processActivationPage` | Click `Change Asset Status` (`Toolbar.AssetStatus`) |
| `activate_select` | same | Select ACTIVE in popup |
| `activate_confirm` / `activate_wait` | same | Confirm; wait until `assetIsActive()` |
| *(done)* | `post-save.js` `afterActivation` | If linked PPMs → `ppm_open_list`; else `finishPostSave` |

**Tab handoff**: `background.js` closes child editor tab, focuses parent, `messages.js` receives `EE_ASSET_EDITOR_CLOSED` and sets `phase: 'activate_open'`.

### 3. PPM loop (per linked workbook row for this Asset Code)

| Phase | Page | Handler | What happens |
|-------|------|---------|--------------|
| `ppm_open_list` | PPM register (parent) | `ppm-register.js` | Click asset PPM nav or `ppmListUrl(entityId)` |
| `ppm_wait_new` | register parent | `ppm-register.js` | Wait for register ready; click Create New |
| `ppm_fill` | `ViewFPPMItem.aspx` (child) | `ppm-editor.js` | Fill PPM fields from workbook |
| `ppm_await_save` | PPM editor | `ppm-editor.js` | Wait for saved PPM URL / entity ID |
| `ppm_status_*` | saved PPM (optional) | `ppm-status.js` | Activate PPM if enabled |
| `ppm_child_closing` | saved PPM | `ppm-status.js` | Close PPM editor child tab |
| `ppm_parent_refresh` / `ppm_parent_refresh_wait` | register parent | `ppm-register.js` | Refresh register; background closes stray children |
| `ppm_next` | register parent | `ppm-register.js` | Increment `ppmIndex`; loop or finish asset |

**Create New (working pattern)** — `ppm-register.js`:
1. Prefer `a[title="Create New"][onclick*="Toolbar.New"]`
2. If button exists but not `visible()` (dropdown menu anchor `.x-button-drop-menu-link`) → call `Toolbar.New()` directly
3. Background detects new child tab → PPM editor opens → phase `ppm_fill`

**PPM parent/child tabs**: background messages `EE_PPM_CURRENT_EDITOR_CLOSED`, `EE_PPM_CHILD_DONE` → parent sets `ppm_parent_refresh_wait` → `ppm_next`.

### 4. Finish asset + next row

`post-save.js` `finishPostSave`:
- No more PPMs → mark asset `saved`, increment `processedThisRun`
- If iteration limit reached or no pending rows → `phase: complete`
- Else if `useSaveAndNew` → `asset_save_and_new` on current saved asset, else `navigate` to new entity URL

### Phase → file quick map

```
engine.js          → routes by phase prefix + page type (isSavedAssetPage, isPpmListPage, etc.)
asset-new.js       → navigate, fill, filling, saving
asset-saved.js     → asset_close_*, activate_*
ppm-register.js    → ppm_open_list, ppm_wait_new, ppm_parent_refresh*, ppm_next
ppm-editor.js      → ppm_fill, ppm_await_save
ppm-status.js      → ppm_status_*, ppm_child_closing
post-save.js       → beginPostSave, afterActivation, finishPostSave, clickSaveTracked
messages.js        → EE_ASSET_EDITOR_CLOSED, EE_PPM_* (resume after background tab ops)
background.js      → ASSET_CLOSE_EDITOR_TAB, PPM child close sweeps, tab focus
```

### Diagnose by failed phase (from diagnostic JSON)

| Failed phase | Likely cause | Check module |
|--------------|--------------|--------------|
| `fill` / `filling` | Field/lookup/tab | `asset-new.js`, `lookup.js`, mappings |
| `await_save` | CAFM validation / save timeout | validation overlay, `saveTimeoutMs` |
| `asset_close_wait` | Editor did not close | `asset-saved.js`, child tab detection in `background.js` |
| `activate_*` | Status popup / ACTIVE selection | `asset-saved.js` |
| `ppm_wait_new` | Create New not found/visible | `ppm-register.js`, `Toolbar.New()` fallback |
| `ppm_fill` / `ppm_await_save` | PPM fields or save | `ppm-editor.js` |
| `ppm_parent_refresh*` | Parent register not refreshed | `ppm-register.js`, background close sweep |

## Patterns to copy (not reinvent)

```javascript
// Page module shape
(() => {
  'use strict';
  const root = globalThis.CAFMImporter;
  const $ = () => root.runtime.b;
  async function processSomething(record) {
    const rt = $();
    // 1. guard current phase + page URL
    // 2. interact via root.core.dom (dispatchClick, visible, waitForDom)
    // 3. rt.addEvent('event-type', { ... });
    // 4. rt.state.session.auto = { ...auto, phase: 'next_phase' };
    // 5. await rt.persistSession(); rt.scheduleAuto(delay);
  }
  root.pages.something = Object.freeze({ processSomething });
})();
```

- **DOM clicks**: `root.core.dom.dispatchClick` — not raw `.click()` unless matching existing code.
- **Toolbar buttons**: `src/core/toolbar.js` for Close/Save; PPM Create New in `src/pages/ppm-register.js` (`a[title="Create New"][onclick*="Toolbar.New"]`, fallback `Toolbar.New()` for `.x-button-drop-menu-link` menu anchors).
- **Logging**: `rt.addEvent(type, payload)` — every state transition and click should be traceable in diagnostic JSON.
- **Timeouts**: `settings.lookupTimeoutMs` / `saveTimeoutMs` are **safety timeouts**, not pacing delays.

## Before adding code — check these first

| Need | Use existing file |
|------|-------------------|
| Page detection / URLs | `src/core/pages.js` |
| Lookup dropdowns | `src/core/lookup.js`, `src/core/lookup-spec.js` |
| Field mappings | `src/data/field-registry.js`, `src/pages/asset-mappings.js` |
| PPM row data | `src/data/ppm.js`, workbook-linked by Asset Code |
| Session / status | `src/data/workbook.js` |
| UI toasts / phase labels | `src/ui/progress-toast.js`, `src/ui/panel.js` |

## Do NOT

- Create parallel orchestrators, polling loops, or duplicate phase state machines.
- Add npm/bundler/TypeScript unless explicitly requested.
- Embed hardcoded asset/PPM templates — data comes from the Excel workbook.
- Fix a `ppm_*` failure by changing `asset_close_*` (or vice versa) without checking the failed phase.
- Skip `await rt.persistSession()` after phase transitions (resume depends on it).

## After workflow changes

Run `node tools/verify-architecture.js` and bump `manifest.json` version if shipping.
